        {
          "moveId": "con-fossils-contingency-unfalsifiability",
          "dimension": "precisionClarity",
          "before": {
            "value": 85,
            "rationale": "The difference between incomplete preservation, evolutionary prediction, and ad hoc guidance is clearly drawn."
          },
          "after": {
            "value": 82,
            "rationale": "The confirmed response clearly distinguishes evidence for evolution from disputes about its tempo, explains the ancestor-survival contingency, and states why a complexity-based God inference is unfalsifiable. Its sequence of fossil, contingency, and historical examples is somewhat sprawling, and the bridge from contingency to the rejection of guidance remains compressed, but the central claims and their scope are readily recoverable without relying on the quarantined segments or garbled names."
          },
