        {
          "moveId": "con-fossils-contingency-unfalsifiability",
          "dimension": "calibrationCharity",
          "before": {
            "value": 75,
            "rationale": "It fairly explains expected gaps, though it treats all proposed guidance as equally unfalsifiable."
          },
          "after": {
            "value": 72,
            "rationale": "Hitchens appropriately separates confidence that evolution occurred from continuing disputes about how it occurred, and he presents contingent ancestor survival as compatible with a theistic interpretation before challenging its evidential force. However, the detour through claims that fossils were planted to test faith emphasizes a weaker creationist response than Boteach's live guided-evolution position, while describing the unfalsifiable guidance inference as effectively no argument at all overstates what the testability objection alone establishes."
          },
