          "before": {
            "value": 58,
            "rationale": "The move discounts the offered preservation explanation and implies a standard of completeness science need not meet."
          },
          "after": {
            "value": 53,
            "rationale": "The response fairly notices that Hitchens described some gaps as only now being filled and presses the scale of the remaining evidential burden. Yet it treats “trillions” of links and their expected ready availability after excavation as established, and it compresses the dispute into slow evolution versus vast leaps. Those emphatic claims exceed what the exchange itself supports, though Boteach does not reject all evolutionary development."
