        {
          "moveId": "con-evolution-tested-and-evidenced",
          "dimension": "evidenceWarrant",
          "before": {
            "value": 82,
            "rationale": "The move cites convergent lines from genetics, selection, fossils, and observation, though details are compressed."
          },
          "after": {
            "value": 71,
            "rationale": "Hitchens gives multiple pertinent examples—testability, influenza sequencing, common ancestry, bacterial origins, and modeled routes for eye development—rather than relying on a bare assertion. Their relevance is mostly compressed rather than explained, “if tested always works” is too absolute, and the connection between influenza sequencing and the full explanatory burden is only sketched, so the passage supplies meaningful but not fully developed warrant."
          },
